g from induced failure of its\n  components, converges back to ready.\n- The deployment works with the platform's standard configuration surfaces (no\n  hand-edited manifests required beyond documented administrator input).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0, managed path): \"administrators can deploy the managed vector\n  store through the Platform Operator with productized images.\"\n\n## Notes\n\n- This epic must not start before Milvus license validation completes: a\n  license failure changes the dependency set and the approach.\n- This epic runs in parallel with the Konflux onboarding of the Milvus build\n  pipeline; the coupling is enforced by the pinned-digest and green-pipeline\n  acceptance criteria above, not by a scheduling dependency.\n- The Platform Operator has no architecture-context file; the implementing team\n  should confirm existing operand-deployment patterns before designing the\n  integration.\n- The Llama Stack provider wiring and the Dashboard deploy-and-manage UI build\n  on the operand/connection surface this epic defines.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":49889,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93a5b4aa5d99853b","agent_id":"aea416225c0a888f0","session_id":"8e36c23f-2012-48a8-9407-9b1658e84980","uuid":"65ea03f7-1db5-48b8-b0dd-6bb4353c9d27","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:24:43.139Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9007 into epics"}
