rface the\n  operator defines).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): \"Llama Stack distributions can consume the chosen vector store\n  as a RAG provider without hand-editing distribution configs\" — managed-path\n  coverage.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Builds on the operand/connection surface defined by the Platform Operator's\n  managed vector store deployment; that surface must exist before this wiring\n  can be built and verified against it.\n- The Llama Stack architecture lists \"Milvus/vector providers for RAG\n  workflows (optional)\" as a dependency — the provider-plugin model exists\n  upstream; this epic productizes the wiring, it does not invent a provider.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50615,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93a5b4aa5d99853b","agent_id":"aea416225c0a888f0","session_id":"8e36c23f-2012-48a8-9407-9b1658e84980","uuid":"edb16253-6130-475b-9d63-df852c435073","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:24:59.099Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9007 into epics"}
