f Milvus repository | Implementation | RHOAI Platform | P0 |\n41\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E003 | License validation for Milvus and transitive dependencies | Implementation | RHOAI Platform | P0 |\n42\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E004 | Konflux build pipeline onboarding for productized Milvus images | Implementation | RHOAI Platform | P0 |\n43\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E005 | Managed vector store deployment via Platform Operator | Implementation | RHOAI Platform | P0 |\n44\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E006 | Llama Stack consumption of managed vector store as RAG provider | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P1 |\n45\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E007 | Dashboard deploy-and-manage UI for managed vector store | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n46\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E008 | Product documentation for managed vector store posture | Implementation | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n47\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E002 | External vector store connection registration and RAG provider consumption | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n48\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E003 | Dashboard connection management UI for external vector stores | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n49\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E004 | Product documentation for external-connection posture | Implementation | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n50\t\n51\tBranch epics are conditional alternatives selected by the outcome of E001; they\n52\tare not standalone main-plan nodes. Main-plan epic count: 1 (E001). Total\n53\tincluding branches: 11.\n54\t\n55\t## Dependency DAG\n56\t\n57\t```mermaid\n58\tgraph TD\n59\t    E001[\"E001 Posture decision - Investigation\"]\n60\t    AE002[\"A-E002 Milvus repo onboarding\"]\n61\t    AE003[\"A-E003 Milvus license validation\"]\n62\t    AE004[\"A-E004 Konflux onboarding\"]\n63\t    AE005[\"A-E005 Operator deploys managed Milvus\"]\n64\t    AE006[\"A-E006 Llama Stack RAG provider wiring\"]\n65\t    AE007[\"A-E007 Dashboard deploy-and-manage UI\"]\n66\t    AE008[\"A-E008 Managed-posture docs\"]\n67\t    BE002[\"B-E002 External connection + consumption\"]\n68\t    BE003[\"B-E003 Dashboard connection UI\"]\n69\t    BE004[\"B-E004 External-posture docs\"]\n70\t\n71\t    E001 --> AE002\n72\t    E001 --> AE003\n73\t    AE002 --> AE004\n74\t    AE003 --> AE005\n75\t    AE005 --> AE006\n76\t    AE005 --> AE007\n77\t    AE002 --> AE008\n78\t    AE003 --> AE008\n79\t    AE004 --> AE008\n80\t    AE005 --> AE008\n81\t    AE006 --> AE008\n82\t    AE007 --> AE008\n83\t    E001 --> BE002\n84\t    BE002 --> BE003\n85\t    E001 --> BE004\n86\t    BE002 --> BE004\n87\t    BE003 --> BE004\n88\t```\n89\t\n90\tArrows point from dependency to dependent. Branch A (managed posture) and\n91\tBranch B (external-connection-only posture) are mutually exclusive conditional\n92\tbranches gated by E001.\n93\t\n94\t## DAG Justification\n95\t\n96\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n97\t|------|------|-----------|\n98\t| E001 → A-E002 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | The posture decision determines whether Milvus is onboarded at all; true gate, action `remove` if the external posture is chosen. |\n99\t| E001 → A-E003 | Rule 3 | Same gate; license validation of Milvus only makes sense in the managed posture. |\n100\t| A-E002 → A-E004 | Rule 5 (repo-onboarding → konflux-onboarding serial) | The Konflux pipeline needs the midstream repository to exist. |\n101\t| A-E003 → A-E005 | Rule 9 (license-validation → general implementation serial) | If Milvus licenses fail, the dependency set and approach change. |\n102\t| (no edge) A-E004 ↔ A-E005 | Rule 10 (konflux ∥ general implementation) | Build config is independent of operator code; coupling is enforced by the \"build pipeline green\" and \"pinned image digest available\" ACs on A-E005, never by a DAG edge. |\n103\t| A-E005 → A-E006 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The operator implementation defines the managed vector store CR/connection surface that Llama Stack provider wiring builds against. |\n104\t| A-E005 → A-E007 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The Dashboard integration reads and writes the CR surface the operator implementation defines. |\n105\t| A-E006 ∥ A-E007 | Rule 14 (different repos, no shared artifacts) | Llama Stack distribution wiring and Dashboard UI are in different repos. |\n106\t| A-E002…A-E007 → A-E008 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by ALL Implementation epics) | Docs describe what was built and must land last. |\n107\t| E001 → B-E002 | Rule 3 | The external registration capability only exists in the external posture; true gate, action `remove` if the managed posture is chosen. |\n108\t| B-E002 → B-E003 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The Dashboard connection UI builds against the connection surface B-E002 defines. |\n109\t| B-E002, B-E003 → B-E004 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by ALL Implementation epics) | Docs last, describing the shipped external posture. |\n110\t\n111\tRule 23 (rollback/feature-flag AC for replaced capability) does not apply: the\n112\tplatform ships no vector store capability today, so nothing is replaced.\n113\t\n114\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n115\t\n116\t| HLR | Priority | Managed-posture coverage (Branch A) | External-posture coverage (Branch B) |\n117\t|-----|----------|-------------------------------------|--------------------------------------|\n118\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 (Investigation) | E001 (Investigation) — shared, posture-agnostic |\n119\t| HLR-2 | P0 | A-E005 (operator deployment of managed store with productized images), enabled by A-E002/A-E003/A-E004 | B-E002 (external connection registration per project with validated connectivity) |\n120\t| HLR-3 | P1 | A-E006 (Llama Stack RAG provider consumption) | B-E002 (consumption without hand-editing distribution configs — same epic: same component, team, and connection surface as the registration capability) |\n121\t| HLR-4 | P1 | A-E007 (deploy-and-manage UI) | B-E003 (connection management UI) |\n122\t| HLR-5 | P2 | A-E008 (docs-authoring) | B-E004 (docs-authoring) |\n123\t\n124\tFull coverage: every HLR maps to at least one epic in each branch; HLR-1 is\n125\tcovered by the shared main-plan Investigation. No orphaned requirements.\n126\tIn Branch B, HLR-2 (P0) and HLR-3 (P1) are deliberately bundled into one epic:\n127\tthey share the same component, team, and connection data structure, so splitting\n128\twould produce two epics building the same surface plus an artificial\n129\tserialization edge. The epic carries the higher priority (P0). In Branch A the\n130\tsame HLRs are separate epics because they belong to different components and\n131\tteams (Platform Operator vs Llama Stack).\n132\t\n133\t## Component Mappings (canonical-name notes)\n134\t\n135\t- **Milvus is not a canonical RHAI Jira component** (not in\n136\t  `.context/rhai-components.txt` and not in architecture context). Its\n137\t  onboarding (A-E002/A-E003/A-E004) and operator deployment (A-E005) epics are\n138\t  filed under the closest canonical component, **Platform Operator** — the\n139\t  component that deploys and lifecycles the managed vector store per HLR-2.\n140\t- **E001** is filed under **Llama Stack**: the RAG consumer whose provider model\n141\t  drives the posture evaluation; no platform-wide component exists in the\n142\t  canonical list.\n143\t- **Docs epics** (A-E008, B-E004) are filed under the canonical\n144\t  **Documentation** component.\n145\t\n146\t## New Component Detection\n147\t\n148\t- **Milvus**: no architecture-context file, not in the canonical component list,\n149\t  and listed in `llama-stack.md` only as an optional external dependency —\n150\t  treated as a new component entering the platform. Per Rule 20 this generates\n151\t  the onboarding chain in Branch A: `repo-onboarding` (A-E002) ∥\n152\t  `license-validation` (A-E003) parallel start → `konflux-onboarding` (A-E004,\n153\t  after repo) → general implementation (A-E005, after license validation,\n154\t  parallel with Konflux onboarding).\n155\t- **Platform Operator**: present in the canonical Jira component list (an\n156\t  existing platform component the strategy assumes can deploy operands), but it\n157\t  has **no architecture-context file**, so its dependency claims could not be\n158\t  validated against architecture context. Flagged as a health warning below; not\n159\t  treated as a repo to onboard.\n160\t\n161\t## Tiered Delivery\n162\t\n163\tNot applicable. The strategy's uncertainty is an internal posture decision with\n164\ttwo bounded outcomes, not an external dependency with uncertain timing — it is\n165\tmodeled as conditional decomposition branches rather than a Tier 1/Tier 2 split.\n166\tEvery branch epic is gated by E001, which is itself the first deliverable (the\n167\tdocumented evaluation and decision required by HLR-1).\n168\t\n169\t## Health Warnings\n170\t\n171\t1. **Missing strategy sections**: no Impacted Teams table, Dependencies table,\n172\t   Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, or NFRs. Teams were inferred — RHOAI\n173\t   GenAI and RHOAI Dashboard from architecture context; **RHOAI Platform**\n174\t   (Platform Operator) and **RHOAI Documentation** (docs epics) are assumptions\n175\t   that need confirmation before planning.\n176\t2. **Platform Operator architecture gap**: no architecture-context file exists\n177\t   for Platform Operator, so the strategy's claim that it can deploy and\n178\t   lifecycle a managed vector store could not be validated against architecture\n179\t   context. Non-blocking (the component is canonical), but the implementing team\n180\t   should confirm operand-deployment patterns.\n181\t3. **Scope trap — \"productized images\"**: HLR-2's \"productized images\" phrase\n182\t   implies the full image productization chain (midstream fork, license\n183\t   clearance, Konflux build pipeline), which the strategy's body never mentions.\n184\t   This is captured as Branch A onboarding epics rather than silently assumed.\n185\t4. **Out-of-scope consistency**: \"shipping both postures in the same release\" is\n186\t   explicitly out of scope, which validates the two-branch conditional\n187\t   structure — the branches must not both be planned for the first release.\n188\t5. **Docs priority note**: HLR-5 is P2, but the docs-authoring epics carry P1\n189\t   via the `docs-authoring` priority exception (strategy frontmatter\n190\t   `priority: Major` → P1). This is by rule, not a priority inversion.\n191\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87f4e20588d33d19","agent_id":"a7ddffbabf94dcc2a","session_id":"8e36c23f-2012-48a8-9407-9b1658e84980","uuid":"ecf95d37-6308-4a4c-b391-0023ba7ddec8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:30:52.108Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-939d7232e1855f90","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
