egistration, connectivity validation, and provider wiring it implies.\n47\t- Record a single decision with rationale, in a reviewable artifact (evaluation\n48\t  document / ADR-style record) attached to the strategy.\n49\t- Identify which downstream capabilities (deployment, Llama Stack provider\n50\t  wiring, Dashboard integration, documentation) are in scope for the first\n51\t  release under the chosen posture.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- A written evaluation exists that compares platform-managed (operator-deployed\n56\t  Milvus) and external-connection-only postures against supportability cost,\n57\t  disconnected-environment viability, and time-to-market, with evidence for\n58\t  each criterion.\n59\t- Exactly one posture is selected and the decision is recorded with rationale\n60\t  sufficient for a stakeholder to review and ratify it.\n61\t- The decision names the downstream capabilities in scope for the first release\n62\t  under the chosen posture, so implementation epics can be planned against it.\n63\t- The evaluation notes which posture-related risks (e.g. image productization\n64\t  effort, license exposure, external-service compatibility) the chosen path\n65\t  accepts and how they are mitigated.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-1 (P0): a decision is reached, with a documented evaluation, on the first\n70\t  supported vector store posture — this epic is the entirety of HLR-1.\n71\t\n72\t## Notes\n73\t\n74\t- The strategy's Out of Scope list forbids shipping both postures in the same\n75\t  release; the decision must pick one.\n76\t- The decision forks HLR-2 through HLR-5 into two conditional implementation\n77\t  branches; the branch plans are attached to this epic's plan document.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87f4e20588d33d19","agent_id":"a7ddffbabf94dcc2a","session_id":"8e36c23f-2012-48a8-9407-9b1658e84980","uuid":"2c2e4e62-c45e-4880-b0ad-1c734216db0c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:30:53.287Z","tool_res