{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-85665c3dfde09aec","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E003\n3\ttitle: License validation for Milvus and transitive dependencies\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9007\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Platform\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: license-validation\n10\tbranch: A\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9007-E001\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9007-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the external-connection-only posture is chosen first, this\n17\t    epic is removed; no Milvus license clearance is needed because the platform does\n18\t    not productize Milvus images.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 0\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# License validation for Milvus and transitive dependencies\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tRuns license scanning and clearance for Milvus and its transitive dependencies\n39\tso the platform can ship productized Milvus images in the managed vector store\n40\tposture. The scan determines whether the dependency set is license-compatible\n41\twith platform productization; a failure here changes the approach or the\n42\tdependency set before operator deployment work proceeds. Applies only if the\n43\tplatform-managed posture is selected.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Run the platform's license scanning process over the pinned upstream Milvus\n48\t  release and its full transitive dependency tree.\n49\t- Check every detected license against the platform's allowed-license policy.\n50\t- Produce a license scan report with a clear pass/fail summary and, for any\n51\t  flagged license, the remediation options (alternative dependency, upstream\n52\t  change, exclusion).\n53\t- Record the clearance decision for the scanned version so image\n54\t  productization can proceed on a known-good basis.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A complete license scan report exists for the pinned Milvus release and its\n59\t  transitive dependencies.\n60\t- Every license found is classified against the platform's allowed-license\n61\t  policy, with the classification traceable in the report.\n62\t- All flagged licenses have documented remediation options, and the overall\n63\t  result is a recorded go/no-go for productizing the scanned version.\n64\t- The scan is reproducible from the recorded inputs (version pin, scanner\n65\t  configuration).\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-2 (P0, managed path): productized images for the managed vector store\n70\t  require a license-cleared dependency set.\n71\t\n72\t## Notes\n73\t\n74\t- This epic runs in parallel with the midstream repository onboarding; it does\n75\t  not wait for the repository to exist (it scans the pinned upstream release).\n76\t- Operator deployment of the managed vector store must not start until this\n77\t  clearance completes, because a license failure changes the dependency set and\n78\t  the approach.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87f4e20588d33d19","agent_id":"a7ddffbabf94dcc2a","session_id":"8e36c23f-2012-48a8-9407-9b1658e84980","uuid":"52aefc6a-2d08-4d0a-a330-bcd004505f36","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:31:01.852Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-85665c3dfde09aec","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
