s configured per\n50\t  distribution), without hand-editing distribution config files.\n51\t- Expose the managed store's connection details to distributions through the\n52\t  platform's standard configuration surfaces rather than manual edits.\n53\t- Verify end-to-end RAG behavior through the distribution: document\n54\t  ingestion and retrieval against the managed store.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A Llama Stack distribution can be brought up using the platform-managed\n59\t  vector store as its RAG vector provider with no hand-edited distribution\n60\t  config files — configuration flows through the platform's standard surfaces.\n61\t- A documented RAG round trip works end to end: documents ingested through the\n62\t  distribution's RAG API are retrievable in queries, backed by the managed\n63\t  store.\n64\t- The provider wiring works against a store deployed through the Platform\n65\t  Operator's managed deployment capability (the operand/connection surface the\n66\t  operator defines).\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-3 (P1): \"Llama Stack distributions can consume the chosen vector store\n71\t  as a RAG provider without hand-editing distribution configs\" — managed-path\n72\t  coverage.\n73\t\n74\t## Notes\n75\t\n76\t- Builds on the operand/connection surface defined by the Platform Operator's\n77\t  managed vector store deployment; that surface must exist before this wiring\n78\t  can be built and verified against it.\n79\t- The Llama Stack architecture lists \"Milvus/vector providers for RAG\n80\t  workflows (optional)\" as a dependency — the provider-plugin model exists\n81\t  upstream; this epic productizes the wiring, it does not invent a provider.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87f4e20588d33d19","agent_id":"a7ddffbabf94dcc2a","session_id":"8e36c23f-2012-48a8-9407-9b1658e84980","uuid":"33ab608b-c9a7-46f8-9a55-495d6b4d2ded","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:31:11.099Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a69