{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a5250de138e4f41","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E002\n3\ttitle: External vector store connection registration and RAG provider consumption\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9007\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9007-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9007-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the platform-managed posture is chosen first, this epic is\n16\t    removed; the managed-path branch deploys the platform vector store and wires Llama\n17\t    Stack to it instead.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 6\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# External vector store connection registration and RAG provider consumption\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tDelivers the external-connection half of HLR-2 together with HLR-3: data\n39\tscientists can register an external vector store connection per project with\n40\tvalidated connectivity, and Llama Stack distributions consume a registered\n41\tconnection as their RAG vector provider without hand-editing distribution\n42\tconfigs. This serves cloud-native customers who already run managed vector\n43\tservices and want a sanctioned way to connect them. Applies only if the\n44\texternal-connection-only posture is selected.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Implement per-project registration of an external vector store connection\n49\t  (endpoint and credentials) through the platform's standard connection\n50\t  surfaces.\n51\t- Validate connectivity at registration time: the platform verifies the\n52\t  registered external store is reachable and usable, and reports validation\n53\t  failures to the registrant.\n54\t- Wire Llama Stack distributions to consume a registered external vector store\n55\t  connection as their RAG vector provider through the distribution's\n56\t  provider-plugin model, without hand-editing distribution config files.\n57\t- Verify end-to-end RAG behavior through the distribution against a registered\n58\t  external store.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- A data scientist can register an external vector store connection in a\n63\t  project, and the registration is scoped to that project.\n64\t- Registration validates connectivity to the external store: a reachable,\n65\t  usable store registers successfully, and an unreachable or unusable one\n66\t  produces an actionable validation failure.\n67\t- A Llama Stack distribution in the project can use the registered connection\n68\t  as its RAG vector provider with no hand-edited distribution config files —\n69\t  configuration flows through the platform's standard surfaces.\n70\t- A documented RAG round trip works end to end against a registered external\n71\t  store: documents ingested through the distribution's RAG API are retrievable\n72\t  in queries.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- HLR-2 (P0, external path): \"data scientists can register an external vector\n77\t  store connection per project with validated connectivity.\"\n78\t- HLR-3 (P1): \"Llama Stack distributions can consume the chosen vector store\n79\t  as a RAG provider without hand-editing distribution configs\" — external-path\n80\t  coverage.\n81\t\n82\t## Notes\n83\t\n84\t- HLR-2 and HLR-3 are bundled into this single epic deliberately: they share\n85\t  the same component, team, and connection data structure, so splitting them\n86\t  would create two epics building the same surface plus an artificial\n87\t  serialization edge. The epic carries the higher priority (P0).\n88\t- The Dashboard connection-management UI builds on the connection surface this\n89\t  epic defines.\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87f4e20588d33d19","agent_id":"a7ddffbabf94dcc2a","session_id":"8e36c23f-2012-48a8-9407-9b1658e84980","uuid":"96d212b8-7fa0-4438-824d-5086565242b3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:31:14.337Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a5250de138e4f41","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
