ace.\n51\t- Implement connection management interactions (create, edit, delete, view\n52\t  connectivity status) against the connection registration capability,\n53\t  including surfacing connectivity validation results to the user.\n54\t- Gate the integration behind the Dashboard's standard per-component feature\n55\t  flag mechanism (OdhDashboardConfig).\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- The Dashboard exposes a connection management UI for external vector store\n60\t  connections: a data scientist can create, edit, view the status of, and\n61\t  delete a per-project connection without using raw YAML or the OpenShift\n62\t  console.\n63\t- Connectivity validation results from the registration capability are visible\n64\t  in the UI, including actionable failure messages for unusable connections.\n65\t- The integration is feature-flagged via the Dashboard's standard config CR\n66\t  and is off by default where the platform requires it.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-4 (P1): \"The Dashboard exposes the chosen integration (... or connection\n71\t  management UI for the external path).\" — external-path coverage.\n72\t\n73\t## Notes\n74\t\n75\t- Depends on the connection surface the external vector store connection\n76\t  registration capability defines; that surface must exist before the UI can\n77\t  be built against it.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87f4e20588d33d19","agent_id":"a7ddffbabf94dcc2a","session_id":"8e36c23f-2012-48a8-9407-9b1658e84980","uuid":"facf15ea-2501-4e5b-b9c4-9046863f038d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:31:20.308Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e025feca244e33f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
