against B-E002's (edge present).\n66\t\n67\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n68\tEvery epic has a single component and single team; no epic spans multiple\n69\tcomponents or teams. No scope duplication: A-E006 (Llama Stack wiring) and\n70\tA-E007 (Dashboard UI) are different repos and surfaces; Branch A and Branch B\n71\tare mutually exclusive conditional alternatives, not coexisting siblings.\n72\tB-E002 correctly merges registration and consumption into one epic rather\n73\tthan splitting one connection surface across two epics. Work-product types\n74\tare not mixed: docs-authoring work (A-E008, B-E004) is separated from code\n75\timplementation. No epic is oversized — each is a bounded, single-sprint-ish\n76\tunit. Milvus onboarding work filed under the canonical Platform Operator\n77\tcomponent is a reasonable and explicitly documented mapping (Milvus is not a\n78\tcanonical component); the validator confirms all components are canonical.\n79\t\n80\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n81\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome (posture choice) determines which\n82\tdownstream epics exist — the definition of a true gate — and all ten branch\n83\tepics depend on it. Every branch epic sets `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-9007-E001`\n84\twith `gate_failure_impact` populated with both `action: remove` and a\n85\tconcrete `fallback_approach` (the opposite branch covers the outcome); the\n86\tgated_by target appears in each epic's direct `dependencies` list. No epic\n87\tlists an Investigation in `dependencies` without `gated_by`. All\n88\tImplementation epics produce concrete artifacts (repository, scan report,\n89\tpipeline config, operator capability, provider wiring, UI, published docs).\n90\tNo misclassifications.\n91\t\n92\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n93\tType-appropriate signal fields throughout: E001 carries the 5-signal\n94\t`investigation_signals`; all ten Implementation epics carry the 9-signal\n95\t`ai_signals` with `investigation_signals: null`. E001's values fit the\n96\tInvestigation rubric: `source_accessibility: 0` correctly reflects that the\n97\tposture decision is a pending product choice not present in any readable\n98\tartifact, and `human_judgment_required: -2` matches a stakeholder\n99\tratification decision. Implementation signal values are consistent with\n100\trationales and strategy content: `human_process_gates: -1` on repo-onboarding\n101\t(org-maintainer approval), license-validation (legal sign-off),\n102\tkonflux-onboarding (tenant provisioning), and docs (review sign-off), with 0\n103\ton general implementation epics; `architecture_claims` correctly\n104\tdifferentiates epics substantiated by architecture context (Llama Stack\n105\tprovider-plugin model, Dashboard integration pattern: 1) from the\n106\tPlatform-Operator gap (0, flagged as unverifiable rather than assumed\n107\tfavorable); `open_questions: 1` is justified because the strategy-level\n108\tunknown is resolved by the gate before each branch runs. All twelve\n109\tai-signals files exist and their rationale values match the frontmatter.\n110\t\n111\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n112\tEvery epic has testable, strategy-derived ACs. Rule-mandated ACs are present\n113\twherever applicable: both docs-authoring epics (A-E008, B-E004) have the\n114\ttechnical-review sign-off AC; the konflux chain has the green-pipeline AC on\n115\tA-E004 and the pinned-digest/green-pipeline AC on A-E005 (Rule 25); both\n116\tDashboard epics have feature-flag (OdhDashboardConfig) ACs. Rollback/feature-\n117\tflag for replacements is correctly N/A — the platform ships no vector store\n118\tcapability today, and the summary records this reasoning. No non-testable\n119\tschedule-constraint ACs were found (no lab-turnaround or review-cadence\n120\tentries misfiled as ACs). No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID —\n121\tbodies refer to capabilities descriptively; all E-number matches are\n122\tfrontmatter fields only.\n123\t\n124\t### 7. Com